From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Matroska display aspect units in the stated direction

DisplayUnit 3 makes DisplayWidth and DisplayHeight the display aspect
ratio. Like the other known units, their ratio must be divided by the
visible picture's ratio to obtain the pixel aspect, not inverted. A
384x288 picture with a 16:9 display ratio needs SAR 4:3, not 3:4.
---
diff --git a/modules/demux/mkv/matroska_segment_parse.cpp b/modules/demux/mkv/matroska_segment_parse.cpp
--- a/modules/demux/mkv/matroska_segment_parse.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/mkv/matroska_segment_parse.cpp
@@ -556,15 +556,12 @@
                     case 0: // pixels
                     case 1: // centimeters
                     case 2: // inches
+                    case 3: // display aspect ratio
+                        // SAR = display aspect / visible picture aspect, for every known unit.
                         vlc_ureduce( &tk->fmt.video.i_sar_num, &tk->fmt.video.i_sar_den,
                                      i_display_width * tk->fmt.video.i_visible_height,
                                      i_display_height * tk->fmt.video.i_visible_width, 0);
                         break;
-                    case 3: // display aspect ratio
-                        vlc_ureduce( &tk->fmt.video.i_sar_num, &tk->fmt.video.i_sar_den,
-                                     i_display_height * tk->fmt.video.i_visible_width,
-                                     i_display_width * tk->fmt.video.i_visible_height, 0);
-                        break;
                 }
             }
         }
